rota lap 4427, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes; advanced past the preceding Fire reading. The three readings surfaced the difference between a declared recovery and files actually present on main, and the value of proving each diagnostic boundary separately.
obs Restored diagnostic script changes from parked commit 93bf141f3. The run_desk function preserves execution-stage exit codes; the decimal scan checks law claims per function. The latest stash adds body-comment claims to that checked set and deduplicates them with doc claims.
obs Reproduced the body-claim fault in an isolated directory under session-output. The expanded control fails two assertions with the old scan and passes all 31 with the repaired scan. The desk control separately passes all 95 assertions.
obs Restored five historical logs with their original bytes: four from the newest automatic stashes and one from the manually named pre-relaunch stash. Their past status fields remain testimony; this record states what this recovery actually lands.
obs The original recovery commit was parked on pier/diverged-20260909-035156. Its latest log and three decimal files were additionally parked in stash zero. All 16 stashes and the recovery branch remain intact.
obs The lexical limit stays parked. The earlier recovery records an eleven-digit zero accepted by the current parser and lexer but rejected by the proposed limit. Leading-zero syntax, token length bounds, and desk-kind declarations remain language custody decisions.
obs Retained Petrichor's published SOURCE.md correction and the current field-only NixOS boundary. The parked manifest addition is superseded here. No public seed was published.
obs The two recovered REDS records retain stamps 20260908.234354 and 20260909.001908. Their unshared numbers were rebound after fetching xy; routing shelves preserve every historical log link. The peer's published row remains unchanged.
obs The cold pass found exactly two reds: four unlanded logs and a recorded glow_decimal_law run whose roster entry was parked with its code. Both causes are included in this recovery. The first detached launch ended without a verdict; the replacement ran to completion with installed Ripgrep on PATH.
obs Older parked source work remains named for recovery: stash ten's declaration-walker coupling repair is absent from main, and stash eleven's self-matching-assert files also need review. Older sample declarations, ELF-header calls, and Mantra changes have later published replacements and are preserved in their stashes.
